31. Independent Verification — Gate E Execution Reconciliation

AOE3 makes a critical distinction between cryptographic authenticity and execution truth.

SIGNED CLAIM is not EXECUTION TRUTH.

A signed record may prove a claim was signed by a key. It does not prove the underlying event occurred exactly as claimed. AOE3 introduces an independent reconciliation layer (Gate E).

```text
AUTHORIZED CLAIM
       |
       v
CONTROLLED EXECUTION
       |
       +----------------------+
       |                      |
       v                      v
CLAIM/EVIDENCE          INDEPENDENT
RECORD                  TELEMETRY
       |                      |
       +----------+-----------+
                  |
                  v
          AOE3 VERIFY / ORACLE
                  |
        MATCH / MISMATCH /
        MISSING / UNKNOWN
```

The verification layer compares the authorized claim against independently observed execution evidence. If required independent evidence is absent, the system must not manufacture verification.

